# Aroundchess


Every time you choose to apply a rule(s), explicitly state the rule(s) in the output. You can abbreviate the rule description to a single word or phrase.

## Project Context
A comprehensive chess training and analysis platform that combines AI technology with personalized learning to help chess players of all levels improve their game. The platform acts as a 24/7 personal chess coach, providing real-time analysis, customized training plans, and detailed performance tracking.

### Key Features of Chess Analyzer:

1. Analysis
- Real-time game evaluation using Stockfish: Instant move analysis by one of the world's strongest chess engines
- Instant feedback on every move: Like having a grandmaster watching over your shoulder
- Detailed explanations of better alternatives: Clear, human-readable explanations of why certain moves are better
- Pattern and mistake identification: Automatically spots recurring themes and errors in your play

2. Learning Tools
- Personalized learning paths: Custom curriculum based on your playing style and goals
- Interactive lessons: Hands-on learning with immediate feedback
- Annotated master games library: Learn from the best games with expert commentary
- Progressive difficulty adaptation: Content that grows with your skill level

3. Practice Exercises
- Tactical puzzles matched to skill level: Challenges that fit your current ability
- Endgame training scenarios: Master crucial endgame positions
- Opening repertoire builder: Develop and practice your preferred openings
- Time management exercises: Learn to use your clock effectively
- AI opponent with adjustable strength: Practice against an engine that matches your level

4. Progress Tracking
- Detailed performance metrics: Comprehensive stats about your chess improvement
- Goal achievement monitoring: Track progress toward your chess objectives
- Skill improvement visualization: Clear graphs showing your development
- Custom progress reports: Personalized feedback on your improvement
- Rating progression tracking: Monitor your rating changes over time

5. Training Programs
- Customized daily/weekly plans: Structured training tailored to your schedule
- Goal-based training paths: Focused exercises to achieve specific objectives
- Weakness-focused exercises: Training targeted at your problem areas
- Adaptive difficulty levels: Challenges that adjust to your progress

6. Game Modes
- Computer play (350-2800 ELO): Face AI opponents of any strength
- Two-player local games: Play face-to-face on the same device
- Online multiplayer: Challenge players worldwide
- Training positions: Practice specific scenarios
- Game analysis mode: Deep dive into any chess position

7. Social Features
- Progress sharing: Show your improvement to friends
- Community interaction: Connect with fellow chess enthusiasts
- Achievement system: Earn rewards for your progress
- Friend challenges: Compete with other players
- Social media integration: Share achievements on your favorite platforms

8. Security & Access
- Two-factor authentication: Extra layer of account protection
- Secure login options: Multiple safe ways to access your account
- Multiple subscription tiers: Choose the plan that fits your needs
- 7-day free trial: Test all premium features without commitment
- Cross-platform access: Use on any device, anywhere


The platform emphasizes user experience with a clean interface, responsive design, and seamless integration of advanced chess training tools with social features.

## Code Style and Structure
- Write concise, technical TypeScript code with accurate examples
- Use functional and declarative programming patterns; avoid classes
- Prefer iteration and modularization over code duplication
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliary verbs (e.g., isLoading, hasError)
- Structure repository files as follows:
```
Aroundchess/
├── app/                # Next.js App Router pages and routes
    ├── auth/           # Authentication related pages
    ├── playground/     # Game modes (computer, two-player, online)
    ├── practice/       # Training and practice features
    ├── analysis/       # Game analysis and statistics
    ├── about/          # About pages
    └── pricing/        # Pricing and subscription pages
├── components/         # Reusable React components
    ├── chess/          # Chess-specific components
    ├── layout/         # Layout components (header, footer)
    ├── ui/             # UI component library
    ├── analysis/       # Analysis-specific components
    └── playground/     # Game mode components
├── lib/                # Core libraries and utilities
    ├── stockfish/      # Stockfish engine integration
    ├── chess/          # Chess game logic
    └── api/            # API utilities
├── utils/              # Helper functions and utilities
    ├── chess/          # Chess-specific utilities
    ├── motion/         # Animation utilities
    └── common/         # Common helper functions
├── store/              # State management
    ├── chess/          # Chess game state
    └── user/           # User preferences state
├── styles/             # Global styles and themes
    └── globals/        # Global CSS
├── public/             # Static assets
    ├── images/         # Image assets
    └── icons/          # Icon assets
├── types/              # TypeScript type definitions
    ├── chess/          # Chess-related types
    └── common/         # Common types
└── config/             # Configuration files
```

